From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] cputlb, target/arm: a page that holds a small MPU region is
 kept but for that region

An MPU region smaller than a target page (1 KiB on M-profile) made every
access to its page look the MPU up again and write its TLB entry again:
get_phys_addr_pmsav7() reported a page size of 0 for any address of a page
that such a region overlaps, and tlb_set_page_full() set TLB_INVALID_MASK
for it.  A guest that guards each thread's stack with a 32-byte region
(the Flipper Zero's firmware) has its interrupt stack, its idle thread's
and every busy thread's stack in such pages, and in a host's reads of a
USB drive that the guest emulates, a third of the vCPU thread's time went
to those refills.

Such a page is kept now but for the part that the small regions cover:
- CPUTLBEntryFull gains sub_lo and sub_hi, the part [sub_lo, sub_hi) of
  the page that the translation is not for (in its tail padding: the
  struct does not grow).  A target sets them with a full page size.
- tlb_set_page_full() gives such an entry TLB_SUBPAGE, a new slow flag:
  every access takes the slow path, and mmu_lookup1() translates one that
  touches the part anew, as on a miss (where a small region's own lookup
  gives the one-access entry that it gave before); any other access is a
  hit, with no lookup.
- probe_access_internal() fills for a probe that touches the part, and
  otherwise returns the flag with the entry, so that no host address is
  given for all of the page (code in such a page is translated as before,
  an instruction at a time); atomic_mmu_lookup() goes serial for an access
  that touches it.
- get_phys_addr_pmsav7() reports the span of the regions that overlap the
  page and that it looked at before the one that matched (or all, with no
  match) as that part, where it reported a page size of 0.  A region that
  holds the address in a disabled subregion and has other subregions in
  the page counts too (it did not before: an entry for the whole page
  could let an access through to an enabled subregion).  A span of the
  whole page is a page size of 0, as before.
- armv7m_nvic.c: what patch 0023 says the TLB holds of an enabled region
  (on which its flushes at the MPU's off and on rest) says so now: the
  page of a smaller region is kept but for it, and the rest of it is the
  default map's, which holds with the MPU off too, or a larger region's,
  whose pages go.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/include/hw/core/cpu.h
+++ b/include/hw/core/cpu.h
@@ -268,6 +268,14 @@
             bool guarded;
         } arm;
     } extra;
+
+    /*
+     * @sub_lo, @sub_hi: the part [sub_lo, sub_hi) of the page, from its
+     * start, that this translation is not for (an MPU region smaller than
+     * a page lies there): an access to it is translated anew.  Both 0:
+     * none.  Only with @lg_page_size of a page or more.
+     */
+    uint16_t sub_lo, sub_hi;
 };
 
